'''Infernal Pegasus Deonil''' (超炎獣テオニール, ''Chō Enjū Teonīru'', '''Super Flame Beast Teonir''') is a [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] variant of [[Angelic Sleipnir]] introduced in [[Empress' Excavation 4]]. It was added in [[Version 12.2 Update|Version 12.2]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Infernal Pegasus Deonil
|image = E 639.png
|first appearance = [[Cursed Flaming Party|Peril in the Volcano III]]<br>[[Empress' Excavation 4]]
|money drop = 2,100¢ - 8,295¢
}}

==Enemy==
Much like Angelic Sleipnir, this nasty enemy boasts extreme health, DPS and attack frequency, which, combined with its extended range and guaranteed [[Mini-Wave]]s render it impervious to most units, [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] or not, in any player's arsenal. Rather than pushing back your units to gain ground, it has a 15% chance to freeze them for 1.67 seconds, which combines with the high damage and constant attacks to often stun-lock cats. The only caveats are its slow movement speed and high knockback count to somehow mitigate its otherwise undisputed dominance. Its immunities to slow and [[Surge Attack|Surges]] aren't that big of a deal, but can still be problematic if they are essential parts of your strategy.

==Strategy==
Just like against [[Berserkory]], [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] can easily stop its advance, but will also double as a stepping stone due to the freeze, allowing Deonil to spam waves, adding thus the necessity for a countermeasure. The same can be said about [[Bondage Cat (Special Cat)|Ultimate Bondage Cat]], who may expect to trigger his Dodge Attack [[Talents|Talent]] a lot with all the Mini-Waves, allowing him to potentially escape the freeze and then disable this enemy with his own.

Unlike in the case of [[Casaurian Ahirujo]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] will struggle to land hits consistently due to range issues, having to rely on lucky dodges or other cats weakening, cursing or freezing Deonil, but can still deal serious damage if he makes it to his target and gets one hit. The only consistent counters are units who outrange it, have a way to deal with Waves (also through another unit) and have some sort of useful ability or good damage ([[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]], [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Togelan Pasalan]], etc.). Despite Deonil's ability to outrange all [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]], some may still be of use, a notable case being [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]] due to having only one knockback, a quick cooldown and resistance to Red enemies. Additionally, [[Hell Warden Emma (Uber Rare Cat)|Hell Commissioner Emma]] can block any Mini-Wave and freeze Deonil does, and, if lucky, can weaken it too, letting your attackers do damage to this nasty enemy.

The [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall]] Decoration and [[Ototo Corps#Waterblast|Waterblast]] Foundation can be combined to reduce damage from both Waves and Red enemies, seriously weakening Deonil's Mini-Waves.

