==Trivia==
*Infernal Pegasus Deonil's mane, fangs, wings, affinity for fire and Japanese name, Teonir, all heavily reference [[wikia:monsterhunter:Teostra|Teostra]], an Elder Dragon in the ''Monster Hunter'' franchise. Its Freeze ability may be based off of the Stun effect that Teostra can inflict in the [[wikia:monsterhunter:Fourth Generation|Fourth Generation]] of ''Monster Hunter'' games, while its [[Mini-Wave]]s may be a substitute for Teostra's explosions, as Deonil was added before the actual [[Explosion]] ability.
*Deonil's English name appears to been mistranslated from its Japanese name, テオニール ''Teonīru'' (Teonir). テ ''Te'' may have been misread as デ ''De'', and the "l" in Deonil was likely supposed to be an "r", since [[Angelic Sleipnir]]'s name also ends in an "r".
*The name De<u>oni</u>l may be partially derived from ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'', a demon-like ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' typically depicted with horns and [[:Category:Red Enemies|red]] or [[:Category:Aku Enemies|blue]] skin.
*Since Angelic Sleipnir is based on [[wikipedia:Sleipnir|Sleipnir]] from Norse mythology, Infernal Pegasus Deonil may represent fellow Norse horse [[wikipedia:Skinfaxi and Hrímfaxi|Skinfaxi]] ("shiny mane"), who pulls the chariot of [[wikipedia:Dagr|Dagr]] (the personification of day) across the sky every morning and illuminates both the sky and Earth with his mane, similar to how Deonil sets both the skies and the ground alight.
*As a fiery horse with draconic wings, Infernal Pegasus Deonil may have been inspired by myths of the Greek Sun god [[wikipedia:Helios|Helios]], whose chariot is said to be pulled by either [https://www.theoi.com/Ther/DrakonesMedea.html dragons] or more commonly a quartet of horses named Pyrois ("The Fiery One"), Aeos ("He of the Dawn"), Aethon ("Blazing") and Phlegon ("Burning").
*Infernal Pegasus Deonil being an aggressive, fiery red horse may reference the [[wikipedia:Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse#Red Horse|Red Horse]] ridden by the second Horseman of the Apocalypse, War; in some translations of the Book of Revelation, his horse's color is specifically a "fiery" red.

